---
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import { property } from "../content/property";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/supporting.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy | Breezy Days OBX"
  description="How Breezy Days OBX uses information submitted with an availability request."
  bodyClass="supporting-page supporting-policy-page"
>
  <SiteHeader />
  <main class="policy-page" id="main-content">
    <article class="policy-card">
      <header class="policy-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">Privacy notice</p>
        <h1>Privacy, in plain language.</h1>
        <p class="policy-updated">Last updated August 18, 2026</p>

        <p class="policy-lede">
          This notice describes the current availability-request process. It is not a rental
          agreement or legal advice; binding stay terms are supplied separately in the
          owner-approved rental agreement.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="policy-section-grid">
        <section>
          <h2>What an availability request includes</h2>
          <p>
            Your requested arrival and departure dates, overnight guest and pet counts, name, email,
            phone number, an optional message, and the two acknowledgements shown on the form.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Why the owners use it</h2>
          <p>
            Those details are used to review availability and guest fit, reply to your request, and
            explain the date-specific price, agreement, and payment steps before you decide whether
            to reserve.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>How the form is handled</h2>
          <p>
            Netlify Forms receives the submission so the owners can review and respond. The form
            does not collect payment information, create an instant booking, or place inquiry data
            in the public owner-settings store.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Analytics and session tools</h2>
          <p>
            Google Analytics 4 and Microsoft Clarity load only when their public project identifiers
            are configured. They are limited to public pages. Form values, dates, contact details,
            and messages are never sent in the site’s custom analytics events, and analytics does
            not run on owner pages.
          </p>
          <p>
            Google Analytics 4 uses cookies and similar identifiers to help the owners understand
            visits and how people find and use the site. Learn{" "}
            <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites"
              >how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a
            >.
          </p>
          <p>
            Microsoft Clarity captures interactions such as clicks, scrolling, heatmaps, and session
            replays so the owners can improve the site. Input fields are masked. Learn more in the{
              " "
            }
            <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement">Microsoft Privacy Statement</a
            >.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Retention, deletion, and binding terms</h2>
          <p>
            Final retention and deletion periods remain subject to owner approval and any applicable
            recordkeeping requirements. They are not rental terms. Email the owners to ask what you
            submitted or request deletion, subject to obligations that may require a record to be
            kept.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Questions about your information</h2>
          <p>
            Email <a href={`mailto:${property.identity.email}`}>{property.identity.email}</a>.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>

      <div class="policy-actions">
        <a class="button" href="/#availability">Check availability</a>
        <a class="text-link" href="/rental-information"
          >Rental information <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a
        >
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
